<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Genevra[Unity]* Are there already plans how to handle massive lag (like in eq), i.e. on weekend days, when more than 2000 people are online?
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Well, some lag is avoidable, and some ain't
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> The internet lag we can't get around, though we hide a lot of it
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> In terms of having servers bog down from too many people, we'll try and keep that from happening by a number of technological ways...
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> ..and also gameplay ways.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Unfortunately (for us:) people like to congregate and that can be bad for server lag
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> However, we've done a lot to make sure that the physics runs efficiently and doesn't bog down too much with lots of people.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Testing will show us a lot of this, and we'll be asking people to crowd into areas to see how well our lag resistance works
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> We also are pretty aggressive about reducing graphics lag - again, a lot of testing to do there too
<br><b>&lt;Vaxhacker&gt;</b> Also, the world map is big, and that means alot of interesting places to explore.  Which spreads the load around, conveniently enough.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *MystiqueDeKami* Will we see spellbooks, scrolls and inscription or will spells be controled solely by having or not having a skill box?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> There will definitely be items in the game that grant spell-like effects - wands, potions and the like
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Many of these things are craftable items as well
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> But be warned, in the wrong hands, they can be non-functional - or dangerous...
