<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> Although you'll probably see some similarities in the moves to the real thing...
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> and we couldn't help but to slip in a little drunken fighting in.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> *hic*
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *SyonarA* Will item drops be randomized, like in UO? or are we going to see more static item generation, like the way rare item drops happen in everquest?
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Our treasure dropping system is extremely flexible.  We can assign any item, or groups of items, to any monster, with any percentage chance of something dropping...
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> It will therefore be predictable in the sense that trolls might rarely drop some troll blood...
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> You won't find troll blood on any old monster, however.  Or you might only find a special sword on a certain TYPE of NPC...
<br>* Gaffer sticks a fork in Windfeather and licks up his blood for the healing properties.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> But it will never be static as in, you can camp the Magic Sword of Whoopass.
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> Our spawn of harvestable resources will be randomized across certain regions as well.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Kypher_East* As far as dying items go... Will it be like current UO where people are running around in out of place colors - the neon pinks, yellows, greens, etc, or will the clothing colors fit the time period? ie: more drab colors for the "older" civilizations, and whatever your creative minds come up with for the newer civilizations?
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Our artists can define palettes for tailor-dyeable pots...
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> So we get to dictate who can dye what which sets of colors
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> So in a word - it's up to our artists/designers what colors they want to be part of the world
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> And we're picky!
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> That being said, our GMs will have the ability to break those rules
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Which they may do to create event prizes and the like.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Pink armor.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Cytris* Are NPC's going to be any different than UO?  Are there any new interesting features about them?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Hmmm, well, for starters, the NPCs will have more dialogue than all of the other Ultimas combined.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> They will also be primarily responsible for questing and skill learning.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Yep, you can say 'Name, Quest, Job AND 'Star Sign'.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> lol Windy
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> However, you have to keep in mind that we are not really interested in creating a perfect NPC sim
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Our game is about players interacting with each other.  The NPCs are there to provide backdrop and context to the world
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Not to define it.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> You will be able to learn much about the world's history from them, if you so choose.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> They're also pretty clever about being able to chase you without 'cheating' - though they will have some tricks up their sleeves if people try to abuse poor defenseless monsters from perching, etc. :)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Oh, yeah, and they'll also be able to get angry with you and ignore you =)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Er, yeah, we'll have some huntable NPCs.  No sense having Scirocco Assassins if you can't be bushwhacked by them now and then.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Magius*  Can you guys release a video of someone fishing off a dock with the new waves????
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> sure, we needed a vacation anyway...
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> oh... you mean, in the game
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> lol
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> Of course, I'd rather see explosion potion fishing.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> hahahah!
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> I was talking to Cynthe about getting some screenies of that before - she's in charge of releasing such things
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Screenshots are a lot easier to make than movies, so we'll probably do some of those first.  Less impressive to look at, but it'll give some idea.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Dunno if fishing poles are in the game yet though :)  But we can do some nice sunsets over the oceans...
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Our skies are spectacular, btw.  Kudos to the engine team again.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Aye, by land, sea, and air, the 3D team kicks ass
<br>* Vaxhacker looks underappreciated
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Er our server side architecture is even more beautiful, but doesn't make for nice screenshots
<br>* Gaffer comforts Vaxhacker*
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> You can see sunsets across seamless server boundaries.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> hahahah
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> lol exactly
<br><b>&lt;Vaxhacker&gt;</b> Indeed you can.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Warrion|UH* What role will rogues play in Origin? Will they be more thieves and pickpockets, or trap disarmers and dungeon sneakers?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> We're really focusing on the adventuring thief.  Skills that exist solely to be antisocial aren't as valuable to a game of this type as skills that help a party to greater rewards
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> The more nefarious abilities of the thief will exist - we have some neat ideas for stealing, thievery, etc - but our emphasis is really in using thieves to make parties stronger.
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> But we do have some stealing should you be inclined. :)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Oh, definitely.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Caperon|NEX* backstab? yay or nay? Will there be more rogue-like abilities?
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> Yup, we're going to have backstabbing.  I'm a big fan of backstabbing.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Ryu_KnT* will we be able to chang ethe music if we wish to do so (not saying we will, just for change :p)
<br>* Ubiq keeps an eye on Mobius. Et tu?
<br>* Gaffer backstabs Mobius with a fork.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> we have put much effort in making the music too cool to want to do that :)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> heheh
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> You can listen to music other than ours, but you won't get the cool effects we do with music (combat music tying in, etc.) with your music...
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> ...mostly because yours may need to be playing from an MP3 player.  You could replace our music files directly, I suppose, but you're better off with a good CD player or MP3 player.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Cause otherwise you'll get unusual effects from our music system.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Our music's cool though - leave it on :)
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Thrilla* Will death be handled in the same ghost type thing
<br><b>&lt;Vaxhacker&gt;</b> OooOOoo
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> No ghosts.  I know it's unpopular to hear, but ghosts were too much work for not enough reward.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Ghosts, by definition, break all of the rules of the game.  This means they are extremely prone to bugs and exploits, which we try to keep as low as possible.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Aye, almost impossible to get all the bugs and wackiness out of ghosts.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Right now we plan to let you speak while dead and laying on the ground, however, so you can get someone to help you out - we will have a resurrection spell of some sort.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Talebearer* On the topic of music, who do we have to thank for the idea of putting "Love is Hell" in the Origin movie?
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> I'm not 100% on this, but Blackthorn (Starr) set that up I believe.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Our sound guy is a former member of the SkateNigs, a local austin Punk Band.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> He happens to be friends with many members of the Thrill Kill Kult, members of which are now part of the Grim Faeries.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Which is the full story, pretty much. =)
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Aye, check out www.grimfaeries.com too.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Listen to Ubiq not me :)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> He has lots of contacts in the industry, so hopefully that will result in cool things for us in the future
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> *Caliban_* Will there be some sort of Epic war to take part in? (order/chaos) if so, how many sides will there be?
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> There will be a strong story, with a strong sense of progress and history, driven by our IGM staff
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> It will have an epic battle that centers on Magic vs. Technology (we wanted to avoid good vs evil)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> With the threat of Adranath and his evil minions looming over all of them.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> The explanation to how we got there is pretty long-winded, but fortunately for you guys, I already wrote it =)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Go to http://www.uo2.com, and read my first letter to the fans.  It explains a lot about the epic war that players will find themselves on the brink of when the game launches.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b>  *Bizzmark* Will we be seeing more of your twisted humor and subliminal messages in Origin, like 'jwilson' slimes and those witty talking crystal balls, among others? ;)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Well now
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> If we told you about them, they wouldn't be easter eggs, would they? =)
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> Trust me, you can't make a game like this without having a sense of humor - or without touching the game with it.
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> We can't promise Easter Eggs at ship.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> I have no idea who was responsible for putting Starr's head on a big egg to replace any objects which can't be loaded as things stand now :)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> That frightened me last weekend.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> So that is truly an easter "egg" indeed :)
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> I tried to put a skeleton on the ground, and I gota big egg with Starr's face on it.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> That's enough to scare anyone
<br><b>&lt;Mobius&gt;</b> I'm suprised you can still world build after that.
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> hell I'm surprised you can still type
<br><b>&lt;Windfeather&gt;</b> Is that going to change?  I put them all over Vesper.
<p><b>&lt;Joshua_Rowan&gt;</b> Okay folks, that just about wraps it up. Thanks to the entire Dev Team for attending and answering all the great questions. And thanks to all of you for participating!
<br><b>&lt;Gaffer&gt;</b> Thanks everyone!  Great questions tonight...
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> The entire team would like to thank you all for coming out.  It's great to see such enthusiasm.  It really validates what we're doing.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> And for what it's worth - there will be a lot more to talk about at the next one.
<br><b>&lt;Ubiq&gt;</b> ;-)


</font>

</td></tr></table>

